Z||000000||Her86GT||06-04-2001||11:58 AM||||Just to give those who need it, some last minute info on the Fiero meet coming this weekend in Grand Bend.  There are about 10 Fieros going and a total of 17 people.  The group continues to grow daily so don't miss out on this. <P> There is a group of us meeting here in London at Springbank Park on Saturday morning at 11:00 and we'll be driving to the Bend together.  All the info is on the thread: Informal Fiero Meet In Grand Bend.<P>If anyone wants any last minute information or last minute help with repairs to their cars, feel free to contact us at (519) 857-2864.  We'll see ya then    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Her86GT (edited 06-04-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||sailordude||06-04-2001||12:46 PM||||The car i just bought is in the shop, but hopefully it will be finished by saturday.  How long will you guys be in Grand Bend.  I'm done work around 1:00, and will drive up after if you are still there.  If I don't see everyone, have a great time, and let me know about the next time you are all going to meet up.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Her86GT||06-04-2001||01:37 PM||||We will be there for a few hours starting in Grand Bend at 1:00.  There will be enough of us there to make it a day.  It would make a good time for pictures and chatting with others about their cars.  This is a rain or shine event so don't be afraid of the weather. A Fiero is worth showing off rain or shine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ||||reg||1
