Z||000008||Huck||06-04-2001||10:04 PM||||Hey guys.  Im in a bad mood.  My mechanic doesn't know what might be wrong with my clutch.  I hope I can still make it to the meet!  He put a new clutch in around sept / oct.  Sat most of the winter (obviously) and then 3 weeks ago my slave goes on me at a stop light. (pissing fluid out the plunger of slave).  I put a new slave in (wagner, aftermarket) and had no luck.  Thinking maybe my master wasn't any good, I changed it too.  Still couldn't build up pressure, and when I did  finally get it good enought to drive, but it faded out after about 3 minutes.  All my mechanic can think of is a faulty slave cylindar, or possible something bent somewhere.  Its not the line, cause I dont lose any fluid, but the rest of thew hydrolics are brand new!!  I wish I knew somebody that had a spare slave for a V6 5spd to try it before I drop another near $200 for another new one!<P>Any idea's anyone??||||reg||1
Z||000009||PBJ||06-04-2001||10:44 PM||||Ahh, that last crunch.  Out in my wife's fiero on sunday and the darn heater core blows  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  so changed it today. <BR>-----------------------------------------<BR>HUCK-sounds like if you keep your foot on the clutch pedal and in gear it will slowly start to engage-this what you mean by fade?<P>If it was the slave it can only fade by leaking fluid externally-this you could see in the boot.<P>IF it was the clutch master it could fade without external leaking.<P>If they are both new than you should have a warranty.<P>It very well could be a bleeding air problem. see other thread in technical re clutch bleeding going on tonight.||||reg||1
